        {
         "tex": "h(2) &= 2 + 1",
         "sym": "2 + 1",
         "new": true
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= 3",
         "sym": "3"
        },
        {
         "tex": "h(3) &= 3 + 1",
         "sym": "3 + 1",
         "new": true
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= 4",
         "sym": "4"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Test injectivity",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "The outputs $2, 3, 4$ are all different, so different inputs give different outputs and $h$ is injective."
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Test surjectivity",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "The codomain is $\\{1, 2, 3, 4\\}$. The element $1$ is not an output, because $x + 1 = 1$ gives $x = 0$, which is not in the domain. So $h$ is not surjective."
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Classify",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "$h$ is injective but not surjective, so it is not bijective. (A bijection needs the same number of elements in the domain and codomain: here $3 \\ne 4$.)"
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "finalAnswer": "h \\text{ is injective, not surjective, so not bijective}"
    },
    "finalSym": "0",
    "answerSym": "floor(Rational(3, 4))"
   }
  ]
